_ai_phoenix_gen_7_full_body_not_a_render.jpg)\n\nThis new update comes less than eight months after we [announced the 
seventh generation of our Phoenix 
robots](https://www.sanctuary.ai/blog/sanctuary-ai-unveils-the-next-generation-of-ai-robotics), highlighting the speed at 
which our team and technology are progressing. Phoenix Generation 8 is designed to be the most versatile and safe way to 
deliver meaningful labor. It has a wheeled base, which is a design decision informed by Sanctuary customer feedback that 
bi-pedal legs are too frail to support a strong torso that is needed to carry out useful work precisely and safely. Key 
improvements include:\n\n*   Improvements to telemetry system for enhanced data capture and training\n\n*   Improvements to
both the depth and vision cameras which increases the field of view and resolution\n\n*   Improvements to Phoenix’s sensor 
suite and audio and video system\n\n*   Improvements in cost savings and design, allowing for increased speed of 
manufacturing and commissioning time\n\nWith this new generation of Phoenix, Sanctuary will be able to provide their AI 
control system with some of the highest quality, highest fidelity training data available. This is a critical step on the 
path to artificial general intelligence. By using detailed training data, it will ground AI in the physical world and 
enable systems to understand and learn from real world experience. Sanctuary general purpose technology is strong, smart, 
